Apply it after the eight patches of the README's REBUILDING list.

The rcbot_mm.dll that ships was built before the forget-on-death and defend_time rules of the
current rcbot-ts-roam.patch / src\bot.cpp. REBUILDING FROM THE CURRENT SOURCE IS THE FIX for citizens
that go for a player again after his respawn. This patch is an extra, for tsrp_rb_forget_cmd 1.

What it adds (CHANGE 8, roaming citizens)
  - "rcbot roamforget <player entity index>": every roaming citizen that holds that player for its
    attacker drops him at once, and with him its current enemy and last enemy. tsrp_roambots.sma sends
    it when tsrp_rb_forget_cmd is 1.

diff --git a/dlls/bot.cpp b/dlls/bot.cpp
index 5297c5c..5a14eae 100644
--- a/dlls/bot.cpp
+++ b/dlls/bot.cpp
@@ -4074,6 +4074,26 @@ edict_t* CBot::RoamAttacker() const
 	return m_pRoamAttacker;
 }
 
+// The plugin's word that a player is to be let off (the server command "rcbot roamforget <index>"): a
+// roamer that holds him for its attacker no longer does, and neither fights nor remembers him. What
+// it was doing about him (turning to face him, a search for where he went) ends by itself: the tasks
+// ask IsEnemy, which is false for him now.
+void CBot::RoamForgetAttacker(const edict_t* pPlayer)
+{
+	if (pPlayer == nullptr || m_pRoamAttacker != pPlayer)
+		return;
+
+	m_pRoamAttacker = nullptr;
+	m_iRoamAttackerId = 0;
+	m_fRoamHurtTime = 0.0f;
+
+	if (m_pEnemy == pPlayer)
+		m_pEnemy = nullptr;
+
+	if (m_pLastEnemy == pPlayer)
+		m_pLastEnemy = nullptr;
+}
+
 // Whom a roamer fights: its attacker, and, while the citizens are insurgents, every player who is
 // not a bot -- or only the players of tsrp_roambots_insurgent_team. Never anything else, not even
 // a door in its way.
